{%- comment -%}
  fye-buybox-eternity — choices for rings whose variants are
  Metal x Diamond Quality: eternity, diamond and gem-set wedding rings.

  Rendered by main-product when the product is NOT a plain band.

  ── THE DATA ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

      Metal            Platinum, 18k Gold, 14k Gold, 9k Gold, Palladium
      Diamond Quality  D/E VVS, F/G VS, G Si, H Si, Lab-grown D VVS

  Both are variant options — 25 variants on a typical eternity ring — and both
  change the price. Gold COLOUR does not change the price, so it is a
  line-item property, not a variant.

  ── THE CONTROL ORDER IS DELIBERATE ───────────────────────────────────────

  Colour first, then carat, matching how someone actually chooses a ring and
  how the plain-band branch already works. Ed, 31/08/2026.

      row 1   Yellow · White · Rose · Platinum · Palladium
      row 2   18k · 14k · 9k          (only when row 1 is a gold)

  That does not map one-to-one onto the data, because "Yellow" is a property
  while "Platinum" is a variant. So every tile in row 1 is a LINK:

    · a gold colour links to the gold variant at the CURRENT carat (or the
      first available), carrying ?gold=Yellow;
    · platinum and palladium link straight to their own variant.

  fye-ui.js reads ?gold= on load, sets the hidden property input and lights the
  right tile. Without JS the property falls back to the first colour, which is
  wrong but harmless — and the alternative, radios, cannot change the variant.

  Carat tiles link to the same colour at another carat, so switching carat
  keeps both the colour and the diamond grade.

  ── PROPERTY NAMES ARE A CONTRACT ─────────────────────────────────────────

  Verbatim from live's product-block.js — the workshop reads these off orders:

      "Gold colour"      "Yellow", not "Yellow Gold"
      "Ring size"
      "Engraving", "Engraving font"
      "_size_surcharge"  "Yes"

  ── ORDER OF THE HIDDEN METAL INPUT ───────────────────────────────────────

  fye-ui.js builds a variant title by joining every [data-fye-option] control
  in DOM order. Shopify's titles are "Metal / Quality", so the hidden metal
  input MUST come before the quality select. It shipped after it once and the
  price silently stopped updating, because "G Si / 18k Gold" matches nothing.

  Parameters: product, settings (the section's), current (chosen variant)
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = settings
  assign p = product

  assign metal_opt = nil
  assign quality_opt = nil
  for option in p.options_with_values
    if option.name == 'Metal'
      assign metal_opt = option
    elsif option.name contains 'Quality'
      assign quality_opt = option
    endif
  endfor

  assign metal_now = metal_opt.selected_value
  assign quality_now = quality_opt.selected_value

  assign is_gold = false
  if metal_now contains 'Gold'
    assign is_gold = true
  endif

  comment
    The carat to aim at when someone picks a gold colour from a non-gold
    metal: keep theirs if they have one, otherwise the first gold offered.
  endcomment
  assign carat_now = ''
  if is_gold
    assign carat_now = metal_now
  else
    for value in metal_opt.values
      if value contains 'Gold'
        assign carat_now = value
        break
      endif
    endfor
  endif

  assign golds = s.gold_colours | default: 'Yellow,White,Rose' | split: ','
  assign sizes = s.ring_sizes | default: 'A,A.5,B,B.5,C,C.5,D,D.5,E,E.5,F,F.5,G,G.5,H,H.5,I,I.5,J,J.5,K,K.5,L,L.5,M,M.5,N,N.5,O,O.5,P,P.5,Q,Q.5,R,R.5,S,S.5,T,T.5,U,U.5,V,V.5,W,W.5,X,X.5,Y,Y.5,Z,Z.5,Z+1,Z+1.5,Z+2,Z+2.5,Z+3,Z+3.5,Z+4,Z+4.5,Z+5,Z+5.5,Z+6,Z+6.5,Z+7,Z+7.5,Z+8,Z+8.5,Z+9,Z+9.5' | split: ','
  assign threshold = s.surcharge_size | default: 'Q'

  comment
    Non-gold metals, in the order the option lists them, so row 1 ends with
    whatever this product actually offers rather than an assumed pair.
  endcomment
  assign plains = ''
  for value in metal_opt.values
    unless value contains 'Gold'
      assign plains = plains | append: value | append: '|'
    endunless
  endfor
  assign plains = plains | split: '|'
-%}

{%- if metal_opt != nil -%}
  {%- comment -%} ---- Row 1: colour ---- {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="pdp__field">
    <p class="pdp__label pdp__label--inline">Metal: <span class="pdp__labelval" data-fye-metal-label>{{ metal_now }}</span></p>

    <ul class="pdp__colours">
      {%- for colour in golds -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign name = colour | strip
          assign tone = name | downcase | prepend: '--metal-18-'
          assign target = nil
          for v in p.variants
            if v.option1 == carat_now and v.option2 == quality_now
              assign target = v
              break
            endif
          endfor
        -%}
        <li>
          {%- if target != nil -%}
            <a class="pdp__colour{% if is_gold and forloop.first %} is-current{% endif %}"
               data-fye-goldtile="{{ name | escape }}"
               style="--sw: var({{ tone }});"
               href="{{ p.url }}?variant={{ target.id }}&gold={{ name | url_encode }}">
              <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
              <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ name }}</span>
            </a>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="pdp__colour is-off" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});">
              <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
              <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ name }}</span>
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}

      {%- for value in plains -%}
        {%- liquid
          assign target = nil
          for v in p.variants
            if v.option1 == value and v.option2 == quality_now
              assign target = v
              break
            endif
          endfor
          if value == 'Platinum'
            assign tone = '--metal-platinum'
          else
            assign tone = '--platinum'
          endif
        -%}
        <li>
          {%- if value == metal_now -%}
            <span class="pdp__colour is-current" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});" aria-current="true">
              <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
              <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ value }}</span>
            </span>
          {%- elsif target != nil -%}
            <a class="pdp__colour" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});" href="{{ p.url }}?variant={{ target.id }}">
              <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
              <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ value }}</span>
            </a>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="pdp__colour is-off" style="--sw: var({{ tone }});">
              <span class="pdp__dot"></span>
              <span class="pdp__colourname">{{ value }}</span>
            </span>
          {%- endif -%}
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%} ---- Row 2: carat, golds only ---- {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if is_gold -%}
    <div class="pdp__field">
      <ul class="pdp__carats">
        {%- for value in metal_opt.values -%}
          {%- if value contains 'Gold' -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign target = nil
              for v in p.variants
                if v.option1 == value and v.option2 == quality_now
                  assign target = v
                  break
                endif
              endfor
              assign label = value | remove: ' Gold' | upcase
            -%}
            <li>
              {%- if value == metal_now -%}
                <span class="pdp__carat is-current" aria-current="true">{{ label }}</span>
              {%- elsif target != nil -%}
                <a class="pdp__carat" href="{{ p.url }}?variant={{ target.id }}" data-fye-keepgold>{{ label }}</a>
              {%- else -%}
                <span class="pdp__carat is-off">{{ label }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </ul>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

  {%- comment -%}
    Carries the gold colour to the cart. Value is set by fye-ui.js from ?gold=;
    disabled on a non-gold so it is not posted at all.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <input type="hidden"
         name="properties[Gold colour]"
         value="{{ golds[0] | strip | escape }}"
         data-fye-gold-input
         {% unless is_gold %}disabled{% endunless %}>

  {%- comment -%} MUST precede the quality select. See the header. {%- endcomment -%}
  <input type="hidden" value="{{ metal_now | escape }}" data-fye-option>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if quality_opt != nil -%}
  <div class="pdp__field">
    <label class="pdp__label" for="pdp-quality">
      {{ quality_opt.name }}
      {%- if s.quality_help_url != blank -%}
        <a class="pdp__sizelink" href="{{ s.quality_help_url }}">What do these mean?</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </label>
    <select class="pdp__select" id="pdp-quality" name="options[{{ quality_opt.name | escape }}]" data-fye-option>
      {%- for value in quality_opt.values -%}
        <option value="{{ value | escape }}"{% if quality_now == value %} selected{% endif %}>{{ value }}</option>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </select>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{%- if sizes.size > 0 -%}
  <div class="pdp__field">
    <label class="pdp__label" for="pdp-size">
      Ring size
      {%- if s.size_guide_url != blank -%}
        <a class="pdp__sizelink" href="{{ s.size_guide_url }}">Find my size</a>
      {%- endif -%}
    </label>
    <select class="pdp__select"
            id="pdp-size"
            name="properties[Ring size]"
            data-fye-size
            data-threshold="{{ threshold }}"
            required>
      <option value="">Select your size</option>
      {%- for size in sizes -%}
        <option>{{ size | strip }}</option>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </select>

    {%- comment -%}
      Enabled by fye-ui.js above the threshold; the cart transform reads it.
      Disabled fields are not posted, so an ordinary size carries no flag.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <input type="hidden" name="properties[_size_surcharge]" value="Yes" data-fye-surcharge disabled>

    <p class="pdp__hint fine" data-fye-surcharge-note hidden>
      {{ s.surcharge_note | default: 'Sizes above Q use more metal, so a 10% surcharge applies. It is shown in the cart.' }}
    </p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
